# Puzzle sources are hashed for provenance, so their bytes must not depend on the
# platform that checked them out. The manifest's `source_sha256` is taken over
# LF-normalised content as well, so a hash is verifiable from any clone; this file
# keeps the working copy matching the blob so the two agree without normalising.
*.rue      text eol=lf
*.clsp     text eol=lf
*.clvm     text eol=lf
*.clvm.hex text eol=lf
*.hex      text eol=lf
*.hash     text eol=lf

# The compiled artefacts and their manifest are compared byte for byte by
# _test_v14_integrity.py.
*.json     text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
